posizioni","cn":null,"fr":"Exposition","sp":"Exhibici\u00f3n","nl":"Tentoonstellingen"}},"others":{"list":[46,36],"translations":{"de":["Multidisziplin\u00e4r","Museen & Kunstzentren"],"pt":[null,null],"en":["Multidisciplinary","Museums and art centers"],"it":["Multidisciplinare","Musei e centri artistici"],"cn":[null,null],"fr":["Pluridisciplinaire","Mus\u00e9es et art centers"],"sp":["Multidisciplinar","Museos y centros de arte"],"nl":["Multidisciplinair","Musea en kunstcentra"]}}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"Back to nature 1900","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.museedelavilledebruxelles.brussels","email":"musea@brucity.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.543825"},"pt":{"name":"Back to nature 1900","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.museedelavilledebruxelles.brussels","email":"musea@brucity.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.543825"},"en":{"name":"Back to nature 1900","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"With this temporary exhibition, the Mus\u00e9e de la Ville de Bruxelles wishes to draw attention to the rich Art Nouveau heritage preserved in the city's collections. These collections are wide and diverse: from embroidery and painting to fashion and architecture. The starting point of the exhibition is the inspiration that artists found in nature at the turn of the century. The subtle aesthetics and powerful lines and shapes of flowers and plants attract attention, as does the sublime representation of women, in all their variations, presented by the artists. The exhibition presents a small but enchanting selection of works, most of which are previously unseen or rarely exhibited.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.museedelavilledebruxelles.brussels","email":"musea@brucity.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.543825"},"it":{"name":"Back to nature 1900","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.museedelavilledebruxelles.brussels","email":"musea@brucity.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.543825"},"cn":{"name":"Back to nature 1900","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.museedelavilledebruxelles.brussels","email":"musea@brucity.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.543825"},"fr":{"name":"Back to nature 1900","shortdescr":"Exposition de cinq oeuvres Art nouveau peu connues du public qui vous plongent dans les rapports de cet art \u00e0 la nature.","longdescr":"Avec cette exposition temporaire, le Mus\u00e9e de la Ville de Bruxelles souhaite attirer l'attention sur le riche patrimoine Art nouveau conserv\u00e9 dans les collections de la ville. Ces collections sont larges et diverses : de la broderie \u00e0 la peinture en passant par l'orf\u00e8vrerie. Le point de d\u00e9part de l'exposition est l'inspiration que les artistes trouvaient dans la nature au d\u00e9but du si\u00e8cle. L'esth\u00e9tique subtile et les lignes et formes puissantes des fleurs et des plantes attirent l'attention, de m\u00eame que la repr\u00e9sentation sublime de la femme, dans toutes ses variations, pr\u00e9sent\u00e9e par les artistes. L\u2019exposition pr\u00e9sente une s\u00e9lection r\u00e9duite mais enchanteresse d\u2019\u0153uvres, dont la plupart sont in\u00e9dites ou rarement expos\u00e9es.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.museedelavilledebruxelles.brussels","email":"musea@brucity.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.543825"},"sp":{"name":"Back to nature 1900","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.museedelavilledebruxelles.brussels","email":"musea@brucity.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.543825"},"nl":{"name":"Back to nature 1900","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"Het Museum van de Stad Brussel wil in deze tijdelijke tentoonstelling de aandacht vestigen op het rijke art nouveau-erfgoed dat in de collecties van de stad wordt bewaard. Die collecties zijn breed en divers: van borduurwerk, over schilderkunst tot mode en architectuur. Het uitgangspunt van de tentoonstelling is de inspiratie die kunstenaars rond de eeuwwisseling vinden in de natuur. Daarbij wordt de aandacht getrokken door de subtiele esthetiek en de krachtige lijnen en vormen van bloemen en planten, maar even goed het sublieme vrouwbeeld, in al haar variaties, dat door kunstenaars naar voor wordt gebracht. ","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.museedelavilledebruxelles.brussels","email":"musea@brucity.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.543825"}},"place":{"id":231543,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Br\u00fcsseler Stadtmuseum - Maison du Roi","address_street_name":"Grand-Place","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.brusselscitymuseum.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Grand-Place","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Das majest\u00e4tische Maison du Roi (dt. Haus des K\u00f6nigs), in dem sich das Br\u00fcsseler Stadtmuseum befindet, ist Teil des architektonischen Ensembles des ber\u00fchmten Grand-Place und z\u00e4hlt zum UNESCO-Weltkulturerbe.\r\n\r\nBei dem neogotischen Geb\u00e4ude, das im 19. Jahrhundert nach den Pl\u00e4nen des Architekten Pierre-Victor Jamaer fertiggestellt wurde, handelt es sich um eine Nachbildung eines Bauwerks im sp\u00e4tgotischen Stil des 16. Jahrhunderts. \r\n\r\nDas hier untergebrachte Br\u00fcsseler Stadtmuseum birgt Ausstellungen und Sammlungen zur Geschichte der Stadt Br\u00fcssel, Stadtentwicklung, Arch\u00e4ologie, Kunst und Stadtleben etc. Auch die Br\u00fcsseler Folklore wird beleuchtet. So ist der Garderobe von Manneken Pis ein eigener Saal gewidmet. Seit Februar 2017 hat sie sogar ein eigenes Museum: GardeRobe MannekenPis an der Rue du Ch\u00eane 19, gleich neben der ber\u00fchmten Brunnenfigur.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e de la Ville de Bruxelles - Maison du Roi","address_street_name":"Grand-Place","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museedelavilledebruxelles.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Grand-Place","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Museum of the City of Brussels","address_street_name":"Grand-Place","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.brusselscitymuseum.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Grand-Place","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Two majestic buildings that stand opposite each other on Brussels' Grand Place have a long-standing rivalry: on one side you have Brussels' City Hall, and on the other the Broodhuis (Bread House), a UNESCO World Heritage Site which houses the Brussels City Museum. The rivalry between these two buildings is no coincidence. In the 15th century, the Duke of Brabant replaced the 13th century wooden bread market building with a prestigious building that would be a symbol of his power and face off against the imposing building on the other side of the Grand Place that symbolised the city's independence. The building owes its French name of Maison du Roi (King's House) to Charles V, Holy Roman Emperor, who once ruled over a large part of the globe and once owned the Bread House. After being destroyed in the 16th century, it was rebuilt in the Gothic Revival style in the 19th century by city architect Victor Jamaer.\r\nBut it's not all about the Broodhuis' history and facade. Inside the Brussels City Museum gives a comprehensive overview of Brussels' history, with particular attention given to the arts, crafts,urbanism and architecture . The original Manneken Pis is also housed here for security reasons, but as for his wardrobe, which is a thousand times larger than even the most passionate fashionista's, you can marvel at that in its dedicated museum on Rue du Ch\u00eane - Eikstraat. \r\n\r\nCombined ticket giving access to  the Brussels City Museum -Maison du Roi and the Garderobe MannekenPis.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"MUSEO DELLA CITTA' DI BRUXELLES - CASA DEL RE","address_street_name":"Grand-Place","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.brusselscitymuseum.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Grand-Place","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Ricostituzione del XIX secolo dell'edificio costruito durante il regno di Carlo V all'inizio del XVI secolo....\r\n\r\n\"Ricostituzione del XIX secolo dell'edificio costruito durante il regno di Carlo V all'inizio del XVI secolo.\r\nMonumento classificato come stile gotico fiammeggiante .\r\nArti plastiche e decorative di Bruxelles: pittura, pale, arazzi, sculture, porcellana, ceramica, argenteria, stagno.\r\nSviluppo urbanistico: mappe, plastici, evocazione dei problemi di comunicazione, delle zone verdi, del porto di Bruxelles, i principali monumenti, le grandi creazioni urbanistiche.\r\nStoria di Bruxelles; le istituzioni politiche locali, il ruolo di Bruxelles quale capitale, la storia economica, sociale, religiosa, culturale ed il folclore (tra cui il guardaroba del Manneken-Pis).\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e de la Ville de Bruxelles - Maison du Roi","address_street_name":"Grand-Place","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museedelavilledebruxelles.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Grand-Place","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"fr":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e de la Ville de Bruxelles \/ Maison du Roi","address_street_name":"Grand-Place","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museedelavilledebruxelles.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Grand-Place","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Faisant face \u00e0 l\u2019H\u00f4tel de Ville gothique, ce magnifique \u00e9difice, b\u00e2ti \u00e0 la fin du 19e si\u00e8cle, profite de la d\u00e9molition de son anc\u00eatre du 16e si\u00e8cle, qui tombe en ruine, pour le remplacer sous la forme d\u2019une reconstitution n\u00e9ogothique, men\u00e9e par l\u2019architecte de la Ville Victor Jamaer. Le souci de perfection dans la reconstitution finira par engendrer un b\u00e2timent id\u00e9alis\u00e9\u2026\r\nL\u2019appellation de l\u2019\u00e9difice appelle quelques explications et contraint \u00e0 un voyage dans le pass\u00e9. D\u00e8s le 13e si\u00e8cle, le site est occup\u00e9 par une halle au pain, construite en bois \u2014 Broodhuis en n\u00e9erlandais, appellation toujours en vigueur dans la langue de Vondel. Le duc de Brabant, propri\u00e9taire des lieux, d\u00e9cide au 15e si\u00e8cle de remplacer cette halle par un \u00e9difice prestigieux, mani\u00e8re pour lui de rappeler son pouvoir en \u00e9rigeant le b\u00e2timent en vis-\u00e0-vis de l\u2019H\u00f4tel de Ville, symbole pour sa part de l\u2019autonomie communale. La d\u00e9signation de \u00ab Maison du Roi \u00bb date du r\u00e8gne de Charles-Quint, \u00e0 la t\u00eate de plusieurs royaumes. Au m\u00eame titre que l\u2019ensemble de la Grand-Place, la Maison du Roi est inscrite au patrimoine mondial de l\u2019UNESCO depuis 2000.\r\nClass\u00e9e dans son enti\u00e8ret\u00e9 en 1936, la Maison du Roi est, depuis 2000, inscrite au patrimoine mondial de l\u2019UNESCO avec l\u2019ensemble de la Grand-Place.\r\nOuvert \u00e0 la fin du 19e si\u00e8cle, le mus\u00e9e de la Ville balaye la longue histoire bruxelloise, en insistant particuli\u00e8rement sur les sph\u00e8res de l\u2019art, de l\u2019artisanat,de l\u2019urbanisme et de l\u2019architecture  . \u00c0 ce dernier titre, une salle enti\u00e8re est d\u00e9di\u00e9e \u00e0 l\u2019histoire de la r\u00e9put\u00e9e statuette du Manneken-Pis, et pr\u00e9sente la statue originale du 17e si\u00e8cle. \u00c0 quelques pas de l\u00e0, vous d\u00e9couvrirez la GardeRobe MannekenPis, une s\u00e9lection de quelques-uns des costumes du ketje, qui en poss\u00e8de pr\u00e8s de 1000 !\r\n\r\nBillet combin\u00e9 donnant acc\u00e8s au Mus\u00e9e de la Ville de Bruxelles - Maison du Roi et \u00e0 la GardeRobe MannekenPis.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"Casa del Rey - Museo de la Ciudad de Bruselas","address_street_name":"Grand-Place","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.brusselscitymuseum.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Grand-Place","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"El Museo de la Ciudad de Bruselas es uno de los tres Premios de los Museos 2014. Ven a visitarlo y descubre por qu\u00e9.\u00a0...\r\n\r\nEl Museo de la Ciudad de Bruselas es uno de los tres Premios de los Museos 2014. Ven a visitarlo y descubre por qu\u00e9.\r\n\r\nUbicado en pleno centro hist\u00f3rico de la ciudad, en la Grand-Place, el Museo de la Ciudad de Bruselas se ha consagrado a la historia y a las artes de la ciudad.\u00a0\r\n\r\nLa versi\u00f3n original del m\u00e1s conocido de los bruselenses, el  Manneken-Pis y su armario, se han conservado magn\u00edficamente en este edificio neog\u00f3tico, declarado Patrimonio Mundial de la Unesco, junto con la Grand-Place.\u00a0\r\nSus colecciones presentan los or\u00edgenes de Bruselas, su desarrollo a lo largo de los siglos y la vida de sus habitantes.\r\nDurante tu visita, podr\u00e1s descubrir objetos arqueol\u00f3gicos, porcelanas, retablos y tapicer\u00edas, grabados, esculturas, pinturas y maquetas de la ciudad.\u00a0\r\n\r\nTe permitir\u00e1n comprender mejor la evoluci\u00f3n de esta capital \u00fanica. En la gran sala de la \u00faltima planta, el museo organiza exposiciones temporales y desvela el fabuloso guardarrop\u00eda de  Manneken-Pis, un tesoro que no te puedes perder.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Museum van de Stad Brussel \/ Broodhuis","address_street_name":"Grote Markt","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museumvandestadbrussel.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Grote Markt","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Op de Grote Markt van Brussel steken twee majestueuze gebouwen elkaar de loef af. Aan de ene kant het Stadhuis van Brussel, er recht tegenover het Broodhuis, UNESCO-werelderfgoed waar het Museum van de Stad Brussel gevestigd is. De rivaliteit tussen de twee gebouwen is geen toeval: de hertog van Brabant verving de 13de eeuwse houten broodhallen \u2013 vandaar de naam Broodhuis - er in de 15de eeuw door een prestigieus gebouw, dat zijn macht in de verf moest zetten en zo tegengewicht moest bieden aan het imposante gebouw aan de overkant, symbool van de stedelijke onafhankelijkheid. De Franse benaming Maison du Roi heeft het gebouw te danken aan Karel V, ooit heerser over een groot deel van de wereld en ook ooit nog eigenaar van het Broodhuis. In de 16de eeuw vernield, werd het op het einde van de 19de eeuw in neogotische stijl heropgebouwd door stadsarchitect Victor Jamaer. \r\nNiet alleen de geschiedenis en de buitenkant van het Broodhuis is de moeite waard. Binnenin geeft het Museum van de Stad Brussel een rijk gestoffeerd overzicht van de geschiedenis van Brussel, met veel aandacht voor kunst, ambachten, stedenbouw en architectuur. Het oorspronkelijke beeldje van Manneken Pis is hier om veiligheidsoverwegingen ook ondergebracht, maar zijn garderobe \u2013 met bijna 1.000 outfits groter dan die van welke fashionista ook \u2013 moet bewonderd worden in het speciaal daarvoor ingerichte museum in de Eikstraat. Veel dichter bij het blote ventje dus.\r\n\r\nEen combiticket geeft toegang tot het Museum van de Stad Brussel-Broodhuis en de Garderobe MannekenPis.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null}},"districts":{"list":[13],"translations":{"de":["Historisches Stadtzentrum"],"pt":[null],"en":["Historical Centre"],"it":["Centro storico"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Centre historique"],"sp":["Centro hist\u00f3rico"],"nl":["Historisch centrum"]}},"zones":{"list":[19],"translations":{"de":["Zentrum"],"pt":[null],"en":["Centre"],"it":["Centro"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Centre"],"sp":["Centro"],"nl":["Centrum"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":958,"location":{"lat":50.8466937,"lon":4.35252339},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2022-11-04T11:47:09+01:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:13:56+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":231543,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Br\u00fcsseler Stadtmuseum - Maison du Roi","address_street_name":"Grand-Place","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.brusselscitymuseum.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Grand-Place","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Das majest\u00e4tische Maison du Roi (dt. Haus des K\u00f6nigs), in dem sich das Br\u00fcsseler Stadtmuseum befindet, ist Teil des architektonischen Ensembles des ber\u00fchmten Grand-Place und z\u00e4hlt zum UNESCO-Weltkulturerbe.\r\n\r\nBei dem neogotischen Geb\u00e4ude, das im 19. Jahrhundert nach den Pl\u00e4nen des Architekten Pierre-Victor Jamaer fertiggestellt wurde, handelt es sich um eine Nachbildung eines Bauwerks im sp\u00e4tgotischen Stil des 16. Jahrhunderts. \r\n\r\nDas hier untergebrachte Br\u00fcsseler Stadtmuseum birgt Ausstellungen und Sammlungen zur Geschichte der Stadt Br\u00fcssel, Stadtentwicklung, Arch\u00e4ologie, Kunst und Stadtleben etc. Auch die Br\u00fcsseler Folklore wird beleuchtet. So ist der Garderobe von Manneken Pis ein eigener Saal gewidmet. Seit Februar 2017 hat sie sogar ein eigenes Museum: GardeRobe MannekenPis an der Rue du Ch\u00eane 19, gleich neben der ber\u00fchmten Brunnenfigur.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e de la Ville de Bruxelles - Maison du Roi","address_street_name":"Grand-Place","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museedelavilledebruxelles.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Grand-Place","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Museum of the City of Brussels","address_street_name":"Grand-Place","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.brusselscitymuseum.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Grand-Place","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Two majestic buildings that stand opposite each other on Brussels' Grand Place have a long-standing rivalry: on one side you have Brussels' City Hall, and on the other the Broodhuis (Bread House), a UNESCO World Heritage Site which houses the Brussels City Museum. The rivalry between these two buildings is no coincidence. In the 15th century, the Duke of Brabant replaced the 13th century wooden bread market building with a prestigious building that would be a symbol of his power and face off against the imposing building on the other side of the Grand Place that symbolised the city's independence. The building owes its French name of Maison du Roi (King's House) to Charles V, Holy Roman Emperor, who once ruled over a large part of the globe and once owned the Bread House. After being destroyed in the 16th century, it was rebuilt in the Gothic Revival style in the 19th century by city architect Victor Jamaer.\r\nBut it's not all about the Broodhuis' history and facade. Inside the Brussels City Museum gives a comprehensive overview of Brussels' history, with particular attention given to the arts, crafts,urbanism and architecture . The original Manneken Pis is also housed here for security reasons, but as for his wardrobe, which is a thousand times larger than even the most passionate fashionista's, you can marvel at that in its dedicated museum on Rue du Ch\u00eane - Eikstraat. \r\n\r\nCombined ticket giving access to  the Brussels City Museum -Maison du Roi and the Garderobe MannekenPis.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"MUSEO DELLA CITTA' DI BRUXELLES - CASA DEL RE","address_street_name":"Grand-Place","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.brusselscitymuseum.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Grand-Place","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Ricostituzione del XIX secolo dell'edificio costruito durante il regno di Carlo V all'inizio del XVI secolo....\r\n\r\n\"Ricostituzione del XIX secolo dell'edificio costruito durante il regno di Carlo V all'inizio del XVI secolo.\r\nMonumento classificato come stile gotico fiammeggiante .\r\nArti plastiche e decorative di Bruxelles: pittura, pale, arazzi, sculture, porcellana, ceramica, argenteria, stagno.\r\nSviluppo urbanistico: mappe, plastici, evocazione dei problemi di comunicazione, delle zone verdi, del porto di Bruxelles, i principali monumenti, le grandi creazioni urbanistiche.\r\nStoria di Bruxelles; le istituzioni politiche locali, il ruolo di Bruxelles quale capitale, la storia economica, sociale, religiosa, culturale ed il folclore (tra cui il guardaroba del Manneken-Pis).\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e de la Ville de Bruxelles - Maison du Roi","address_street_name":"Grand-Place","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museedelavilledebruxelles.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Grand-Place","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"fr":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e de la Ville de Bruxelles \/ Maison du Roi","address_street_name":"Grand-Place","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museedelavilledebruxelles.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Grand-Place","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Faisant face \u00e0 l\u2019H\u00f4tel de Ville gothique, ce magnifique \u00e9difice, b\u00e2ti \u00e0 la fin du 19e si\u00e8cle, profite de la d\u00e9molition de son anc\u00eatre du 16e si\u00e8cle, qui tombe en ruine, pour le remplacer sous la forme d\u2019une reconstitution n\u00e9ogothique, men\u00e9e par l\u2019architecte de la Ville Victor Jamaer. Le souci de perfection dans la reconstitution finira par engendrer un b\u00e2timent id\u00e9alis\u00e9\u2026\r\nL\u2019appellation de l\u2019\u00e9difice appelle quelques explications et contraint \u00e0 un voyage dans le pass\u00e9. D\u00e8s le 13e si\u00e8cle, le site est occup\u00e9 par une halle au pain, construite en bois \u2014 Broodhuis en n\u00e9erlandais, appellation toujours en vigueur dans la langue de Vondel. Le duc de Brabant, propri\u00e9taire des lieux, d\u00e9cide au 15e si\u00e8cle de remplacer cette halle par un \u00e9difice prestigieux, mani\u00e8re pour lui de rappeler son pouvoir en \u00e9rigeant le b\u00e2timent en vis-\u00e0-vis de l\u2019H\u00f4tel de Ville, symbole pour sa part de l\u2019autonomie communale. La d\u00e9signation de \u00ab Maison du Roi \u00bb date du r\u00e8gne de Charles-Quint, \u00e0 la t\u00eate de plusieurs royaumes. Au m\u00eame titre que l\u2019ensemble de la Grand-Place, la Maison du Roi est inscrite au patrimoine mondial de l\u2019UNESCO depuis 2000.\r\nClass\u00e9e dans son enti\u00e8ret\u00e9 en 1936, la Maison du Roi est, depuis 2000, inscrite au patrimoine mondial de l\u2019UNESCO avec l\u2019ensemble de la Grand-Place.\r\nOuvert \u00e0 la fin du 19e si\u00e8cle, le mus\u00e9e de la Ville balaye la longue histoire bruxelloise, en insistant particuli\u00e8rement sur les sph\u00e8res de l\u2019art, de l\u2019artisanat,de l\u2019urbanisme et de l\u2019architecture  . \u00c0 ce dernier titre, une salle enti\u00e8re est d\u00e9di\u00e9e \u00e0 l\u2019histoire de la r\u00e9put\u00e9e statuette du Manneken-Pis, et pr\u00e9sente la statue originale du 17e si\u00e8cle. \u00c0 quelques pas de l\u00e0, vous d\u00e9couvrirez la GardeRobe MannekenPis, une s\u00e9lection de quelques-uns des costumes du ketje, qui en poss\u00e8de pr\u00e8s de 1000 !\r\n\r\nBillet combin\u00e9 donnant acc\u00e8s au Mus\u00e9e de la Ville de Bruxelles - Maison du Roi et \u00e0 la GardeRobe MannekenPis.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"Casa del Rey - Museo de la Ciudad de Bruselas","address_street_name":"Grand-Place","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.brusselscitymuseum.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 50","phone_booking":"+32 2 279 43 67","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Grand-Place","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"El Museo de la Ciudad de Bruselas es uno de los tres Premios de los Museos 2014. Ven a visitarlo y descubre por qu\u0