"Exposition","sp":"Exhibici\u00f3n","nl":"Tentoonstellingen"}},"others":{}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"\"Artificialia\", Stephan Balleux","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.fondationblan.org\/","email":"info@fondationblan.org","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50000167"},"pt":{"name":"\"Artificialia\", Stephan Balleux","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.fondationblan.org\/","email":"info@fondationblan.org","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50000167"},"en":{"name":"\"Artificialia\", Stephan Balleux","shortdescr":"Until September 2023, discover the exhibition \"Artificialia\" by the Belgian artist Stephan Balleux, who has taken over the entire building with new works linked to older ones from his oeuvre.","longdescr":"The townhouse occupied by the blan foundation is strangely reminiscent of the architectural images artist Stephan Balleux has worked on for years. These images, picked up in bookshops or on the street, are an essential source of reflection and activation in his work. For him, collecting them is the first artistic act. The exhibition occupies the three floors of the foundation in the manner of a cabinet of curiosities; \"Artificialia\" is, in fact, the name given to collections of objects designed, manufactured or modified by man. The exhibition begins on the first floor, with a light and airy display of very recent works, in constant dialogue with the architecture of the building and with an emphasis on large-format paintings. This first tour ends in a room where four strangely similar figures, surrounded by the living, encircle the viewer in a movement that turns the gaze around: but who's looking at whom? In counterpoint, the journey through the cellars, functional and full of machines and pipes, is placed under the sign of profusion. Each room and passageway can be seen as a specific cabinet of curiosities (that of existence, of the organic and the fluid, of space turned pictorial, of genealogy, of the obscure, of our relationship to the living, to almost nothing, to the cult of painting). Every nook and cranny is taken up. The three self-lit display cases created especially for the occasion, which bear the exhibition title, act as powerful stimulants for our ability to create meaning from scattered fragments. It is called watching.","performers":"Stephan Balleux","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.fondationblan.org\/","email":"info@fondationblan.org","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50000167"},"it":{"name":"\"Artificialia\", Stephan Balleux","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.fondationblan.org\/","email":"info@fondationblan.org","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50000167"},"cn":{"name":"\"Artificialia\", Stephan Balleux","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.fondationblan.org\/","email":"info@fondationblan.org","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50000167"},"fr":{"name":"\"Artificialia\", Stephan Balleux","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.fondationblan.org\/","email":"info@fondationblan.org","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50000167"},"sp":{"name":"\"Artificialia\", Stephan Balleux","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.fondationblan.org