first, second, third, fourth and last fridays of the month from 19:00 to 23:00"}}],"targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"educational_targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"tags":["major_event","exterior"]},{"id":50001735,"date_start":"2023-09-08","date_end":"2023-11-19","date_next":"2023-09-08","accept_article27":false,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":false,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":true,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"last_updated_at":"2023-09-04T08:45:02+02:00","published_at":"2023-09-04T08:34:29+02:00","publication_state":"public","date_embargo":null,"show_in_agenda":true,"is_outside":false,"is_high_capacity":false,"is_not_major_event":false,"backoffice_id":284631,"facebook_link":null,"import_origin":null,"is_part_of":null,"sub_type":"expo","ranking":0.2392722755946373,"languages":{"spoken":["fr","en","nl"],"subtitles":[]},"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"de":"Ausstellung","pt":null,"en":"Exhibition","it":"Esposizioni","cn":null,"fr":"Exposition","sp":"Exhibici\u00f3n","nl":"Tentoonstellingen"}},"others":{"list":[24],"translations":{"de":["Kunstgalerien"],"pt":[null],"en":["Art Galleries"],"it":["Gallerie d'arte"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Galeries d'art"],"sp":["Galer\u00edas de arte"],"nl":["Galeries"]}}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"Season XXVII- Ann Beate Tempelhaug Solo Show, Nord","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/spazionobile.com\/","email":"lc@spazionobile.com","phone_contact":"+32 475 53 19 88","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001735"},"pt":{"name":"Season XXVII- Ann Beate Tempelhaug Solo Show, Nord","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/spazionobile.com\/","email":"lc@spazionobile.com","phone_contact":"+32 475 53 19 88","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001735"},"en":{"name":"Season XXVII- Ann Beate Tempelhaug Solo Show, Nord","shortdescr":"This first solo show by Norwegian artist Ann Beate Tempelhaug at Spazio Nobile Gallery opens a new chapter in the artist\u2019s career that has spanned over forty years. The gallery is presenting a series of some fifteen new works painted in \/ on life-sized ceramic objects, strong and vivid immersions that call for subtle feelings and visually tactile sensations.","longdescr":"Her freely shaped and sculpted ceramic pieces are entirely hand-painted, both on their surface and on their edges, reflecting her curiosity and desire to investigate the duality of beauty and the meaning of life through colours and shapes.\n\nShe pushes the limits inherent to ceramics as a medium of creation, and challenges format and weight to reach the feasible in what could be perceived as impossible. All is connected in her art process, the sculptural qualities and the painterly quality melt together as an entireness. Slightly concave surfaces and waves depict the upheavals of time and life. This exploration in the materiality allows her to merge artistic intentions into stories about existence.\n\nImmersed in her own singular universe, Ann Beate Tempelhaug dedicates this exhibition Nord to the great Nordic landscapes and the energy flow they provide her. The abstraction of her porcelain glazed works captures the attention and fascinates the eye. Since she was a child, her desire has been to create \u201cthese large formats that are bigger\u201d than herself, no doubt as a way of reaching a threshold of spirituality that belongs to her only, and which she wants to share with us. And for connecting herself stronger to life and to art. \u201cAs a child, I remember this huge mountain (\u00d8yfjellet) outside our kitchen window. I had to see the entire mountain, and to be able to, I had to move very close to the window, which I did every day.\u201d\n\nTempelhaug paints without knowing the final result of her glazes before firing. Working for days on end in her studio at the porcelain factory (NTP) in Norway, she releases her emotions against a backdrop of inner landscapes whose intensity follows the infinite line of jazz (Nils Petter Moldv\u00e6r, Arve Henriksen, Jan Bang, among others), classic or Piazzolla\u2019s liberated tango, a music she is particularly fond of when she sets to work and which transports to another places, as if in a creative trance. She plunges into her deepest feelings, treating them with successive brushstrokes of varying thickness. Her expressionist paintings are impregnated with colours that reveal themselves after the long five days of firing at 1300oC. They are surging waves of \u201cchiaroscuro\u201d, of dazzling light, sometimes polar and wintry, sometimes solar and summery, that invade the porcelain-enamelled stoneware mural. Fragile, often weakened by the heat of the kiln. Not all of her large sculptures reach us \u2013 that\u2019s the mystery and risk of the ceramic firing process. Her husband and her lover, Eirik Gjedrem, also a ceramist, accompanies her on this artistic and existential adventure like a guardian angel. He is her main assistant during the heavy and complexed creation processes of her works.\n\nNord will feature a selection of new large-scale works created during the first part of 2023 including: Beyond (Bortenfor), Milonga, Mirage (Luftspeiling), Mostly North (Det meste er Nord), Into Love (Inn i kj\u00e6rlighet), Oblivion (Glemsel), Prelude (Forspill), Polar Light (Nordlys), Twilight (Skumring), Umbra\u2026  \u2013  along with smaller, more intimate works with rounded, organic contours like In-Out, which transport us into another space-time, both lyrical and metaphysical. The impression is of emerging from nothingness and feeling at one with a lake, a forest, a sky drowning in deep water, in an immensity as far as the eye can see. Each of these extraordinarily powerful paintings expresses, in its own way, the artist\u2019s strong and profound emotions, reflecting her life\u2019s journeys and her quest for transcendence.  \u201cI am moved by nature, but I don\u2019t feel directly linked to a movement of painters who work with nature as a subject or a medium\u201d.  In a free, abstract expressionism, Tempelhaug uses her pictorial art as catharsis.\n\nLise Coirier, August 2023.\n\n","performers":"Ann Beate Tempelhaug","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/spazionobile.com\/","email":"lc@spazionobile.com","phone_contact":"+32 475 53 19 88","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001735"},"it":{"name":"Season XXVII- Ann Beate Tempelhaug Solo Show, Nord","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/spazionobile.com\/","email":"lc@spazionobile.com","phone_contact":"+32 475 53 19 88","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001735"},"cn":{"name":"Season XXVII- Ann Beate Tempelhaug Solo Show, Nord","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/spazionobile.com\/","email":"lc@spazionobile.com","phone_contact":"+32 475 53 19 88","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001735"},"fr":{"name":"Season XXVII- Ann Beate Tempelhaug Solo Show, Nord","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/spazionobile.com\/","email":"lc@spazionobile.com","phone_contact":"+32 475 53 19 88","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001735"},"sp":{"name":"Season XXVII- Ann Beate Tempelhaug Solo Show, Nord","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/spazionobile.com\/","email":"lc@spazionobile.com","phone_contact":"+32 475 53 19 88","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001735"},"nl":{"name":"Season XXVII- Ann Beate Tempelhaug Solo Show, Nord","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/spazionobile.com\/","email":"lc@spazionobile.com","phone_contact":"+32 475 53 19 88","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001735"}},"place":{"id":265998,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Spazio Nobile Gallery, Contemporary Applied Arts","address_street_name":"Rue Franz Merjay","address_street_number":"142","address_street_box":null,"email":"lc@spazionobile.com","website":"http:\/\/www.spazionobilegallery.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 768 25 10","phone_booking":"+32 475 53 19 88","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue Franz Merjay, 142","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"Spazio Nobile Gallery, Contemporary Applied Arts","address_street_name":"Rue Franz Merjay","address_street_number":"142","address_street_box":null,"email":"lc@spazionobile.com","website":"http:\/\/www.spazionobilegallery.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 768 25 10","phone_booking":"+32 475 53 19 88","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue Franz Merjay, 142","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Spazio Nobile Gallery, Contemporary Applied Arts","address_street_name":"Rue Franz Merjay","address_street_number":"142","address_street_box":null,"email":"lc@spazionobile.com","website":"http:\/\/www.spazionobilegallery.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 768 25 10","phone_booking":"+32 475 53 19 88","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue Franz Merjay, 142","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"Spazio Nobile Gallery for applied art, design and photography..\r\nA space dedicated to culture and creation\r\n\r\nHighlighting expertise in design and the applied arts (glass, metal, wood, ceramic, etc.) as well as in photography, Spazio Nobile Gallery aims to create a dialogue between diverse disciplines; a harmonious melange of contemporaneity and sense of history.\r\n\r\nSpazio Nobile Gallery is the shared project of a couple made up of two art historians who have taken complementary paths in their own lives. With more than 20-years in the field of art and design, Lise Coirier has focussed her career on spotlighting designers who infuse matter with form and life. Her husband, Gian Giuseppe Simeone, followed a parallel journey, concentrating on the preservation of cultural and artistic heritage but also public awareness.\r\n","description_print":"Spazio Nobile Gallery for applied art, design and photography opens its doors.\r\nA space dedicated to culture and creation\r\n\r\nHighlighting expertise in design and the applied arts (glass, metal, wood, ceramic, etc.) as well as in photography, Spazio Nobile aims to create a dialogue between diverse disciplines; a harmonious melange of contemporaneity and sense of history.\r\n\r\nSpazio Nobile is the shared project of a couple made up of two art historians who have taken complementary paths in their own lives. With more than 20-years in the field of art and design, Lise Coirier has focussed her career on spotlighting designers who infuse matter with form and life. Her husband, Gian Giuseppe Simeone, followed a parallel journey, concentrating on the preservation of cultural and artistic heritage but also public awareness.\r\n\r\n","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Spazio Nobile Gallery, Contemporary Applied Arts","address_street_name":"Rue Franz Merjay","address_street_number":"142","address_street_box":null,"email":"lc@spazionobile.com","website":"http:\/\/www.spazionobilegallery.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 768 25 10","phone_booking":"+32 475 53 19 88","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue Franz Merjay, 142","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"Spazio Nobile Gallery, Contemporary Applied Arts","address_street_name":"Rue Franz Merjay","address_street_number":"142","address_street_box":null,"email":"lc@spazionobile.com","website":"http:\/\/www.spazionobilegallery.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 768 25 10","phone_booking":"+32 475 53 19 88","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue Franz Merjay, 142","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"fr":{"name":"Spazio Nobile Gallery, Contemporary Applied Arts","address_street_name":"Rue Franz Merjay","address_street_number":"142","address_street_box":null,"email":"lc@spazionobile.com","website":"http:\/\/www.spazionobilegallery.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 768 25 10","phone_booking":"+32 475 53 19 88","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue Franz Merjay, 142","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"Spazio Nobile Gallery, la galerie d\u2019arts appliqu\u00e9s, de design et de photographie.\r\nUn espace d\u00e9di\u00e9 \u00e0 la culture de la cr\u00e9ation\r\n\r\nMettant \u00e0 l\u2019honneur la cr\u00e9ation et le savoir-faire tant dans le design et les arts appliqu\u00e9s (verre, m\u00e9tal, bois, c\u00e9ramique\u2026) que dans la photographie, Spazio Nobile a pour ambition de faire dialoguer ces diff\u00e9rentes disciplines en m\u00ealant harmonieusement la contemporan\u00e9it\u00e9 et le sensde l\u2019histoire.\r\n\r\nSpazio Nobile Gallery, c\u2019est tout d\u2019abord le projet partag\u00e9 d\u2019un couple d\u2019historiens de l\u2019art aux parcours on ne peut plus compl\u00e9mentaires. Active depuis plus de 20 ans dans le domaine du design et de la cr\u00e9ation, Lise Coirier s\u2019investit depuis le d\u00e9but de sa carri\u00e8re pour mettre en \u00e9vidence ces cr\u00e9ateurs qui insufflent forme et vie \u00e0 la mati\u00e8re. Son mari, Gian Giuseppe Simeone, suit une voie parall\u00e8le, ax\u00e9e davantage sur la sauvegarde et la mise en valeur du patrimoine culturel et artistique, ainsi que leur diffusion vers les publics.\r\n\r\n","description_print":"Spazio Nobile Gallery, la galerie d\u2019arts appliqu\u00e9s, de design et de photographie.\r\nUn espace d\u00e9di\u00e9 \u00e0 la culture de la cr\u00e9ation\r\n\r\nMettant \u00e0 l\u2019honneur la cr\u00e9ation et le savoir-faire tant dans le design et les arts appliqu\u00e9s (verre, m\u00e9tal, bois, c\u00e9ramique\u2026) que dans la photographie, Spazio Nobile a pour ambition de faire dialoguer ces diff\u00e9rentes disciplines en m\u00ealant harmonieusement la contemporan\u00e9it\u00e9 et le sensde l\u2019histoire.\r\n\r\nSpazio Nobile, c\u2019est tout d\u2019abord le projet partag\u00e9 d\u2019un couple d\u2019historiens de l\u2019art aux parcours on ne peut plus compl\u00e9mentaires. Active depuis plus de 20 ans dans le domaine du design et de la cr\u00e9ation, Lise Coirier s\u2019investit depuis le d\u00e9but de sa carri\u00e8re pour mettre en \u00e9vidence ces cr\u00e9ateurs qui insufflent forme et vie \u00e0 la mati\u00e8re. Son mari, Gian Giuseppe Simeone, suit une voie parall\u00e8le, ax\u00e9e davantage sur la sauvegarde et la mise en valeur du patrimoine culturel et artistique, ainsi que leur diffusion vers les publics.\r\n","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"Spazio Nobile Gallery, Contemporary Applied Arts","address_street_name":"Rue Franz Merjay","address_street_number":"142","address_street_box":null,"email":"lc@spazionobile.com","website":"http:\/\/www.spazionobilegallery.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 768 25 10","phone_booking":"+32 475 53 19 88","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue Franz Merjay, 142","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Spazio Nobile Gallery, Contemporary Applied Arts","address_street_name":"Franz Merjaystraat","address_street_number":"142","address_street_box":null,"email":"lc@spazionobile.com","website":"http:\/\/www.spazionobilegallery.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 768 25 10","phone_booking":"+32 475 53 19 88","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Franz Merjaystraat, 142","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"Spazio Nobile Gallery, de Galerij voor toegepaste kunst, design en fotografie.\r\nEen oase gewijd aan de cultuur van het cre\u00ebren. \r\n\r\nSpazio Nobile Gallery ambieert een oord van kruisbestuiving en dialoog tussen de verschillende\r\ndisciplines design, toegepaste kunst ( metaal, glas, hout en keramiek ) en fotografie, waarbij het accent gelegd wordt op creatie en know-how, en heden en verleden harmonieus samenvloeien.\r\n\r\nSpazio Nobile Gallery is in de eerste plaats het gezamenlijke project van een uiterst complementair koppel kunsthistorici. Lise Coirier is reeds meer dan 20 jaar actief in de wereld van design en creatie. Sinds het begin van haar carri\u00e8re ijvert ze om de ontwerpers, die de materie vorm en leven inblazen, in het voetlicht te plaatsen. Haar echtgenoot Gian Giuseppe Simeone volgt een gelijkaardig traject, maar richt zich eerder op het behoud en de waardering van het artistieke en culturele patrimonium, en hun publieke verspreiding. \r\n","description_print":"Spazio Nobile Gallery, de Galerij voor toegepaste kunst, design en fotografie.\r\nEen plek gewijd aan de cultuur van het cre\u00ebren. \r\n\r\nSpazio Nobile ambieert een oord van kruisbestuiving en dialoog tussen de verschillende\r\ndisciplines design, toegepaste kunst ( metaal, glas, hout en keramiek ) en fotografie, waarbij het accent gelegd wordt op creatie en know-how, en heden en verleden harmonieus samenvloeien.\r\n\r\nSpazio Nobile is in de eerste plaats het gezamenlijke project van een uiterst complementair koppel kunsthistorici. Lise Coirier is reeds meer dan 20 jaar actief in de wereld van design en creatie. Sinds het begin van haar carri\u00e8re ijvert ze om de ontwerpers, die de materie vorm en leven inblazen, in het voetlicht te plaatsen. Haar echtgenoot Gian Giuseppe Simeone volgt een gelijkaardig traject, maar richt zich eerder op het behoud en de waardering van het artistieke en culturele patrimonium, en hun publieke verspreiding. \r\n\r\nMeer dan een \u201cgalerij\u201d in de gewone zin van het woord, wenst Spazio Nobile een plaats te worden waar werk en leven in elkaar overvloeien, waar kennis wordt uitgewisseld, een\r\nesthetische confrontatie opgevat als een volwaardige culturele en zintuigelijke ervaring.","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null}},"districts":{"list":[6],"translations":{"de":["Chatelain\/Bailli"],"pt":[null],"en":["Chatelain\/Bailli"],"it":["Chatelain\/Bailli"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Chatelain\/Bailli"],"sp":["Ch\u00e2telain\/Bailli"],"nl":["Kasteleinswijk\/Baljuw"]}},"zones":{"list":[21],"translations":{"de":["S\u00fcden"],"pt":[null],"en":["South"],"it":["Sud"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Sud"],"sp":["Sur"],"nl":["Zuid"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":25998,"location":{"lat":50.81667529,"lon":4.35208305},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2022-06-18T18:04:01+02:00","published_at":"2016-06-03T14:55:14+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":false,"is_in_vb_export":false,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":265998,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Spazio Nobile Gallery, Contemporary Applied Arts","address_street_name":"Rue Franz Merjay","address_street_number":"142","address_street_box":null,"email":"lc@spazionobile.com","website":"http:\/\/www.spazionobilegallery.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 768 25 10","phone_booking":"+32 475 53 19 88","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue Franz Merjay, 142","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"Spazio Nobile Gallery, Contemporary Applied Arts","address_street_name":"Rue Franz Merjay","address_street_number":"142","address_street_box":null,"email":"lc@spazionobile.com","website":"http:\/\/www.spazionobilegallery.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 768 25 10","phone_booking":"+32 475 53 19 88","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue Franz Merjay, 142","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Spazio Nobile Gallery, Contemporary Applied Arts","address_street_name":"Rue Franz Merjay","address_street_number":"142","address_street_box":null,"email":"lc@spazionobile.com","website":"http:\/\/www.spazionobilegallery.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 768 25 10","phone_booking":"+32 475 53 19 88","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue Franz Merjay, 142","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":"Spazio Nobile Gallery for applied art, design and photography..\r\nA space dedicated to culture and creation\r\n\r\nHighlighting expertise in design and the applied arts (glass, metal, wood, ceramic, etc.) as well as in photography, Spazio Nobile Gallery aims to create a dialogue between diverse disciplines; a harmonious melange of contemporaneity and sense of history.\r\n\r\nSpazio Nobile Gallery is the shared project of a couple made up of two art historians who have taken complementary paths in their own lives. With more than 20-years in the field of art and design, Lise Coirier has focussed her career on spotlighting designers who infuse matter with form and life. Her husband, Gian Giuseppe Simeone, followed a parallel journey, concentrating on the preservation of cultural and artistic heritage but also public awareness.\r\n","description_print":"Spazio Nobile Gallery for applied art, design and photography opens its doors.\r\nA space dedicated to culture and creation\r\n\r\nHighlighting expertise in design and the applied arts (glass, metal, wood, ceramic, etc.) as well as in photography, Spazio Nobile aims to create a dialogue between diverse disciplines; a harmonious melange of contemporaneity and sense of history.\r\n\r\nSpazio Nobile is the shared project of a couple made up of two art historians who have taken complementary paths in their own lives. With more than 20-years in the field of art and design, Lise Coirier has focussed her career on spotlighting designers who infuse matter with form and life. Her husband, Gian Giuseppe Simeone, followed a parallel journey, concentrating on the preservation of cultural and artistic heritage but also public awareness.\r\n\r\n","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Spazio Nobile Gallery, Contemporary Applied Arts","address_street_name":"Rue Franz Merjay","address_street_number":"142","address_street_box":null,"email":"lc@spazionobile.com","website":"http:\/\/www.spazionobilegallery.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 768 25 10","phone_booking":"+32 475 53 19 88","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue Franz Merjay, 142","address_line2":"1050 Ixelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"Spazio Nobile Gallery, Contemporary Applied Arts","address_street_name":"Rue Franz Merjay","address_street_number":"142","address_street_box":null,"email":"lc@spazionobile.com","website":"http:\/\/www.spazionobilegallery.com","phone_contact":"+32 2 768 25 10","phone_booking":"+32 475 53 19 88","address_zip":"1050","address_city":"Ixelles","address_line1":"Rue Franz Merjay, 142","address_l