artisanales de 10 pays diff\u00e9rents seront pr\u00e9sentes. Au total, 56 bi\u00e8res \u00e0 go\u00fbter, sans oublier la musique, les food trucks, et des surprises ! D'ailleurs, BBP f\u00eate ses 10 ans cette ann\u00e9e... Alors soyez pr\u00eat.es pour une c\u00e9l\u00e9bration en plein air pleine de promesses!","longdescr":null,"performers":"Organisateur : Brussels Beer Project\nBrasseries pr\u00e9sentes : \nKyoto Brewing Co. (Japon)\nTo \u00d8l (Danemark)\n\u00c0 tue-t\u00eate! (Suisse)\nSiren Craft Brew (UK)\nBrekeriet (Su\u00e9dois)\nLa Pirata Brewing (Espagne)\nCervecera Pen\u00ednsula (Espagne)\nSenses Brewing (France)\nBRLO (Allemagne)\nKaapse Brouwers (Pays-Bas)\nDOK Brewing (Belge)\nBrasserie Surrealiste (Belge)\nBrussels Beer Project (Belge)\nDANSAERT (Belge)","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/beerproject.be\/pages\/wanderlust-23","email":"keepintouch@beerproject.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001629"},"sp":{"name":"WANDERLUST - craft beer festival","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/beerproject.be\/pages\/wanderlust-23","email":"keepintouch@beerproject.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001629"},"nl":{"name":"WANDERLUST - craft beer festival","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/beerproject.be\/pages\/wanderlust-23","email":"keepintouch@beerproject.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001629"}},"place":{"id":1613,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Alter Hafen, March\u00e9 aux Poissons (Fischmarkt)  ","address_street_name":"Quai aux Briques","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Quai aux Briques","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Der Hafen von Br\u00fcssel erstreckte sich einst bis ins Herz der Stadt, wobei eine Drehbr\u00fccke das Bassin des Barques vom Bassin des Marchands trennte. Auf den langen Kaianlagen mit ihrem pulsierenden Leben wurden die Gesch\u00e4fte abgewickelt. Der Ort, der traditionell mit dem Verkauf von Fisch in Verbindung gebracht wurde, befand sich in der N\u00e4he der heutigen Kirche Sainte-Catherine. Von 1884 bis 1955 gab es hier einen Markt namens \u201eVismet\".   \r\n\r\nNoch heute lassen der Quai au Bois \u00e0 Br\u00fbler und der Quai aux Briques, die den March\u00e9 aux Poissons umgeben, die einstig emsige Wirtschafts-, Lebensmittel- und Gastronomiet\u00e4tigkeit erahnen. Der Hafen war an dieser Stelle bis Anfang des 20. Jahrhunderts aktiv, dann wurden die Becken zugesch\u00fcttet. An ihrer Stelle wurde zwischen 1854 und 1874 die Kirche Sainte-Catherine errichtet. Heutzutage findet hier zwar kein Fischmarkt mehr statt, doch seit einigen Jahrzehnten hat sich der Platz als Hochburg f\u00fcr Fisch- und Schalentierrestaurant etabliert.  ","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"Ancien port, March\u00e9 aux Poissons","address_street_name":"Quai aux Briques","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Quai aux Briques","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Old Port, fish market","address_street_name":"Quai aux Briques","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Quai aux Briques","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"The port of Brussels used to extend right into the heart of the city. A swing bridge separated the Bassin des Barques from the Bassin des Marchands. It was on these long quays that business was conducted. The site, traditionally associated with the sale of fish, is located near Saint Catherine\u2019s Church. A market called \"Vismet\" was active there from 1884 to 1955. \r\n\r\nEven today, the Quai au Bois \u00e0 Br\u00fbler and the Quai aux Briques, which surround the March\u00e9 aux Poissons, bear witness to abundant economic, food and gastronomic activity. Port activities continued at this location until the beginning of the 20th century, when the basins were filled in. Saint Catherine\u2019s Church was built on the site of the Sainte-Catherine basin between 1854 and 1874. There is no fish market there now, but for decades the site has been a mecca for fish and shellfish restaurants in the capital.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Ancien port, March\u00e9 aux Poissons","address_street_name":"Quai aux Briques","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Quai aux Briques","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"Ancien port, March\u00e9 aux Poissons","address_street_name":"Quai aux Briques","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Quai aux Briques","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"fr":{"name":"Ancien port, March\u00e9 aux Poissons","address_street_name":"Quai aux Briques","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Quai aux Briques","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Le port de Bruxelles arrivait jadis vraiment jusqu\u2019au c\u0153ur de la ville. Un pont tournant s\u00e9parait le Bassin des Barques du Bassin des Marchands. C\u2019est sur ces longs quais que les affaires se faisaient et que l\u2019animation battait son plein. Le lieu, traditionnellement associ\u00e9 \u00e0 la vente de poissons, se situe pr\u00e8s de l\u2019actuelle \u00c9glise Sainte-Catherine. Un march\u00e9 appel\u00e9 le \u00ab Vismet \u00bb y fut actif de 1884 \u00e0 1955. \r\n\r\nAujourd\u2019hui encore, le Quai au Bois \u00e0 Br\u00fbler et le Quai aux Briques, qui entourent le March\u00e9 aux Poissons, t\u00e9moignent d\u2019une riche activit\u00e9 \u00e9conomique, alimentaire et gastronomique. Les activit\u00e9s portuaires ont exist\u00e9 \u00e0 cet endroit jusqu\u2019au d\u00e9but du XXe si\u00e8cle puis les bassins ont \u00e9t\u00e9 combl\u00e9s. L\u2019\u00c9glise Sainte-Catherine a, quant \u00e0 elle, \u00e9t\u00e9 \u00e9difi\u00e9e \u00e0 l\u2019emplacement du Bassin Sainte-Catherine, entre 1854 et 1874. De nos jours, il ne s'y tient plus de march\u00e9 aux poissons mais depuis des d\u00e9cennies l'endroit est le haut-lieu des restaurants \u00e0 poisson et crustac\u00e9s de la capitale.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"Ancien port, March\u00e9 aux Poissons","address_street_name":"Quai aux Briques","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Quai aux Briques","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Oude haven, Vismarkt ","address_street_name":"Baksteenkaai","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Baksteenkaai","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"De haven van Brussel reikte vroeger tot in het hart van de stad, met een draaibrug die het Schuitendok van het Handelsdok scheidde. Op de langgerekte kades vlakbij de huidige Sint-Katelijnekerk werd volop handel gedreven en was er bedrijvigheid alom. Van 1884 tot 1995 kon je er steevast terecht om vis te kopen op de \u2018Vismet.\u2019 \r\n\r\nDe huidige Vismarkt, omringd door de Brandhoutkaai en de Baksteenkaai, bruist ook vandaag nog van activiteit, met voeding en gastronomie voorop. Havenactiviteit is er niet meer: de bekkens werden begin 20ste eeuw gedempt, en tussen 1854 en 1874 werd de Sint-Katelijnekerk gebouwd op het oude Sint-Katelijnebekken. Tegenwoordig is er ook geen echte vismarkt meer, maar al sinds decennia is deze plek het mekka van de vis- en schaaldierenrestaurants in Brussel. ","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null}},"districts":{"list":[3],"translations":{"de":["Dansaert\/Sainte-Catherine"],"pt":[null],"en":["Dansaert\/Sainte-Catherine"],"it":["Dansaert\/Sainte-Catherine"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Dansaert\/Sainte-Catherine"],"sp":["Dansaert\/Sainte-Catherine"],"nl":["Dansaertwijk\/Sint-Katelijne"]}},"zones":{"list":[19],"translations":{"de":["Zentrum"],"pt":[null],"en":["Centre"],"it":["Centro"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Centre"],"sp":["Centro"],"nl":["Centrum"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":207,"location":{"lat":50.85193861,"lon":4.34803516},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2022-10-10T10:25:09+02:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:13:21+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":false,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":266293,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Brussels Beer Project","address_street_name":"Rue Antoine Dansaert","address_street_number":"188","address_street_box":null,"email":"keepintouch@beerproject.be","website":"http:\/\/www.beerproject.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue Antoine Dansaert, 188","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"Brussels Beer Project","address_street_name":"Rue Antoine Dansaert","address_street_number":"188","address_street_box":null,"email":"keepintouch@beerproject.be","website":"http:\/\/www.beerproject.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue Antoine Dansaert, 188","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Brussels Beer Project","address_street_name":"Antoine Dansaert","address_street_number":"188","address_street_box":null,"email":"keepintouch@beerproject.be","website":"http:\/\/www.beerproject.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Antoine Dansaert, 188","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"This young Brussels company offers atypical beers created in participation with a community of passionate beer lovers. Since a few years, a new wave has come up - bold, creative, collaborative - that challenges the idea of flavours and taste. Professional brewers from around the world are welcome in Brussels to create new flavours and push the boundaries of beer. On the menu: the whole spectrum from Russian Imperial Stouts to a mix of \u2018Old School\u2019 Belgian with influences from the New World. The all stars are : Delta, Saison IPA \u2013 a tropical view on Brussels; Dark Sister, Black IPA - maleficent sister of the Delta; Grosse Bertha, Belgian Hefeweizen - a Weizenbeer for adults and the Babylone, Bread Bitter - the first beer brewed with recycled bread. Brussels Beer Project breaths contemporary Brussels, a cosmopolitan city that lives and evolves.","description_print":"This young Brussels company offers atypical beers created in participation with a community of passionate beer lovers. Since a few years, a new wave has come up - bold, creative, collaborative - that challenges the idea of flavours and taste. Professional brewers from around the world are welcome in Brussels to create new flavours and push the boundaries of beer. On the menu: the whole spectrum from Russian Imperial Stouts to a mix of \u2018Old School\u2019 Belgian with influences from the New World. The all stars are : Delta, Saison IPA \u2013 a tropical view on Brussels; Dark Sister, Black IPA - maleficent sister of the Delta; Grosse Bertha, Belgian Hefeweizen - a Weizenbeer for adults and the Babylone, Bread Bitter - the first beer brewed with recycled bread. Brussels Beer Project breaths contemporary Brussels, a cosmopolitan city that lives and evolves.","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Brussels Beer Project","address_street_name":"Rue Antoine Dansaert","address_street_number":"188","address_street_box":null,"email":"keepintouch@beerproject.be","website":"http:\/\/www.beerproject.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue Antoine Dansaert, 188","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"Brussels Beer Project","address_street_name":"Rue Antoine Dansaert","address_street_number":"188","address_street_box":null,"email":"keepintouch@beerproject.be","website":"http:\/\/www.beerproject.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue Antoine Dansaert, 188","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"fr":{"name":"Brussels Beer Project","address_street_name":"Rue Antoine Dansaert","address_street_number":"188","address_street_box":null,"email":"keepintouch@beerproject.be","website":"http:\/\/www.beerproject.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue Antoine Dansaert, 188","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Cette jeune entreprise bruxelloise propose des bi\u00e8res atypiques cr\u00e9\u00e9es en partenariat avec une communaut\u00e9 de passionn\u00e9s amateurs de bi\u00e8re. Depuis quelques ann\u00e9es, une nouvelle vague est arriv\u00e9e \u2013 audacieuse, cr\u00e9ative, collaborative \u2013 qui chamboule les standards des saveurs et du go\u00fbt. Des ma\u00eetres brasseurs du monde entier sont invit\u00e9s \u00e0 Bruxelles pour co-cr\u00e9er de nouveaux go\u00fbts.  Au menu : un \u00e9ventail complet commen\u00e7ant avec les stouts imp\u00e9riales russes jusqu\u2019\u00e0 un m\u00e9lange d\u2019\u00ab Old School \u00bb belge influenc\u00e9e par des saveurs du Nouveau Monde. Les all stars sont : la Delta, Saison IPA - une vue exotique de Bruxelles ; la Dark Sister, Black IPA - la s\u0153ur mal\u00e9fique de la Delta ; la Grosse Bertha, Belgian Hefeweizen - une Weizen pour adulte et la Babylone, Bread Bitter - 1\u00e8re bi\u00e8re brass\u00e9e \u00e0 partir de pain frais recycl\u00e9. Le Brussels Beer Project repr\u00e9sente Bruxelles contemporaine, une ville cosmopolite vivante et en \u00e9volution.","description_print":"Cette jeune entreprise bruxelloise propose des bi\u00e8res atypiques cr\u00e9\u00e9es en partenariat avec une communaut\u00e9 de passionn\u00e9s amateurs de bi\u00e8re. Depuis quelques ann\u00e9es, une nouvelle vague est arriv\u00e9e \u2013 audacieuse, cr\u00e9ative, collaborative \u2013 qui chamboule les standards des saveurs et du go\u00fbt. Des ma\u00eetres brasseurs du monde entier sont invit\u00e9s \u00e0 Bruxelles pour co-cr\u00e9er de nouveaux go\u00fbts.  Au menu : un \u00e9ventail complet commen\u00e7ant avec les stouts imp\u00e9riales russes jusqu\u2019\u00e0 un m\u00e9lange d\u2019\u00ab Old School \u00bb belge influenc\u00e9e par des saveurs du Nouveau Monde. Les all stars sont : la Delta, Saison IPA - une vue exotique de Bruxelles ; la Dark Sister, Black IPA - la s\u0153ur mal\u00e9fique de la Delta ; la Grosse Bertha, Belgian Hefeweizen - une Weizen pour adulte et la Babylone, Bread Bitter - 1\u00e8re bi\u00e8re brass\u00e9e \u00e0 partir de pain frais recycl\u00e9. Le Brussels Beer Project repr\u00e9sente Bruxelles contemporaine, une ville cosmopolite vivante et en \u00e9volution.","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"Brussels Beer Project","address_street_name":"Rue Antoine Dansaert","address_street_number":"188","address_street_box":null,"email":"keepintouch@beerproject.be","website":"http:\/\/www.beerproject.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue Antoine Dansaert, 188","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Brussels Beer Project","address_street_name":"Antoine Dansaertstraat","address_street_number":"188","address_street_box":null,"email":"keepintouch@beerproject.be","website":"http:\/\/www.beerproject.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Antoine Dansaertstraat, 188","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Deze jonge Brusselse onderneming biedt atypische bieren aan die gecre\u00eberd worden in samenspraak met een gemeenschap van gepassioneerde bierliefhebbers. Sinds een aantal jaren is er een nieuwe wind komen waaien - gedurfd, gewaagd en creatief - die het idee van smaak durft uitdagen. Professionele brouwers vanuit de hele wereld zijn in Brussel welkom om nieuwe smaken te cre\u00ebren en grenzen af te tasten. Op het menu staat: het hele spectrum van Russische Imperial Stout tot een mix van \u2018Old School\u2019 Belgische smaken met invloeden uit de Nieuwe Wereld. De all stars zijn: de Delta, Saison IPA - een tropisch zicht op Brussel ; de Dark Sister, Black IPA \u2013 de onheilspellende zus van de Delta ; de Grosse Bertha, Belgian Hefeweizen - een Weizen voor volwassenen en de Babylone, Bread Bitter- het eerste bier gebrouwd met gerecycleerd brood. Brussels Beer Project is een uiting van de frisse hedendaagse wind die door het cosmopolitische Brussel waait. ","description_print":"Deze jonge Brusselse onderneming biedt atypische bieren aan die gecre\u00eberd worden in samenspraak met een gemeenschap van gepassioneerde bierliefhebbers. Sinds een aantal jaren is er een nieuwe wind komen waaien - gedurfd, gewaagd en creatief - die het idee van smaak durft uitdagen. Professionele brouwers vanuit de hele wereld zijn in Brussel welkom om nieuwe smaken te cre\u00ebren en grenzen af te tasten. Op het menu staat: het hele spectrum van Russische Imperial Stout tot een mix van \u2018Old School\u2019 Belgische smaken met invloeden uit de Nieuwe Wereld. De all stars zijn: de Delta, Saison IPA - een tropisch zicht op Brussel ; de Dark Sister, Black IPA \u2013 de onheilspellende zus van de Delta ; de Grosse Bertha, Belgian Hefeweizen - een Weizen voor volwassenen en de Babylone, Bread Bitter- het eerste bier gebrouwd met gerecycleerd brood. Brussels Beer Project is een uiting van de frisse hedendaagse wind die door het cosmopolitische Brussel waait. ","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"region":"brussels","backoffice_id":26293,"location":{"lat":50.85275676,"lon":4.34190956},"last_upda