office_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/fb.me\/e\/634vBejhF","email":"medexmuseum@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001733"},"pt":{"name":"WORKSHOP + CONCERT \u00b7 Across Hungarian borders : Roma re-creation with words & Music from Transylvania","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/fb.me\/e\/634vBejhF","email":"medexmuseum@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001733"},"en":{"name":"Across Hungarian borders : Roma re-creation with words & Music from Transylvania","shortdescr":"On Friday 15th September, let's cross the borders of a monolithic Hungarian identity with a workshop around languages and identity, followed by two concerts that will bring us on a journey to Transylvania, exploring the Hungarian subculture of Romania ! ","longdescr":"18.00 \u00b7 Decolonial poem writing workshop : a Hungarian-Roma (re)creation with words with Marina Csik\u00f3s (IN ENGLISH) \n\nThis workshop is for everyone who has ever found themselves in the position of \"in-betweeness\" and internal conflicts of languages, cultures, identities, places and feelings. \n\nDuration : 2 hours \u00b7 Free participation \u00b7 Register by email : medexmuseum(at)gmail.com\n\n\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\n\n20.30 \u00b7 CONCERT-OPENING : La Farkas, songwriting in Hungarian by Csilla De\u00e0k\n\n21.00 \u00b7 CONCERT - T\u00c0NCH\u00c0Z : \"Outside the borders: Hungarian Music from Transylvania\"\n\nTransylvania (\"Erd\u00e9ly\" in Hungarian) is a region of Romania, home of an important Hungarian minority, whose traditional music is very popular in Hungary. Since the 70s, Budapest people favor Erd\u00e9lyi tunes in their t\u00e0nch\u00e0z (folk balls). The band will present some of the most beautiful songs of this acclaimed repertoire : some songs to cry, many songs to dance, come and enjoy this music with us ! \n\nWith : Nicolas Hauzeur (violin, BE) \u00b7 Vilmos Csikos (double-bass, HU) \u00b7 J\u00e9r\u00e9mie B\u00e9nichou (br\u00e0cs, FR) \u00b7 Csilla De\u00e0k (singer & song-writer, HU-FR)\n\nEntrance to the concert : pay what you can \u00b7 prix libre\n\nMore info on the facebook event : https:\/\/fb.me\/e\/634vBejhF  ","performers":"Marina Csik\u00f3s ; Csilla Deak (singer & song-writer) ; Nicolas Hauzeur (violin) ; Vilmos Csikos (doubl-bass) ; J\u00e9r\u00e9mie B\u00e9nichou (br\u00e0cs) ","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/fb.me\/e\/634vBejhF","email":"medexmuseum@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001733"},"it":{"name":"WORKSHOP + CONCERT \u00b7 Across Hungarian borders : Roma re-creation with words & Music from Transylvania","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/fb.me\/e\/634vBejhF","email":"medexmuseum@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001733"},"cn":{"name":"WORKSHOP + CONCERT \u00b7 Across Hungarian borders : Roma re-creation with words & Music from Transylvania","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/fb.me\/e\/634vBejhF","email":"medexmuseum@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001733"},"fr":{"name":"A travers les fronti\u00e8res hongroises","shortdescr":"Vendredi 15 septembre, on traverse les fronti\u00e8res d'une identit\u00e9 hongroise monolithe avec un workshop autour des th\u00e9matiques de la langue & de l'identit\u00e9 (en anglais) suivi de deux concerts qui nous feront voyager en Transylvanie, \u00e0 la d\u00e9couverte de la culture musicale de la communaut\u00e9 hongroise de Roumanie. ","longdescr":"18.00 \u00b7 Atelier d'\u00e9criture de po\u00e8mes d\u00e9coloniaux : un re-cr\u00e9ation de l'identit\u00e9 hongroise-rom avec Marina Csik\u00f3s (IN ENGLISH) \n\nCe workshop s'adresse \u00e0 tou\u00b7te\u00b7s celleux qui se sont d\u00e9j\u00e0 trouv\u00e9\u00b7e\u00b7s en position \"d'entre-deux\", qui ont ressenti un conflit interne entre deux langues, deux cultures, deux territoires, deux identit\u00e9s... \n\nDur\u00e9e : 2 heures \u00b7 participation gratuite \u00b7 inscription par email : medexmuseum(a)gmail.com\n\n\n20.30 \u00b7 CONCERT-OPENING : La Farkas, chansons hongroises par Csilla De\u00e0k\n\n21.00 \u00b7 CONCERT - T\u00c0NCH\u00c0Z : \"Par-del\u00e0 les fronti\u00e8res : musique hongroise de Transylvanie\" \n\nLa Transylvanie (\"Erd\u00e9ly\" en hongrois) est une r\u00e9gion de la Roumanie o\u00f9 vit une importante communaut\u00e9 hongroise, dont la musique traditionnelle est tr\u00e8s populaire en Hongrie. Depuis les ann\u00e9es 70, les habitants de Budapest adorent danser au rythme \"erd\u00e9lyi\" lors de bals populaires (t\u00e0nch\u00e0z). Le quatuor compos\u00e9 par Csilla De\u00e0k (chant), Nicolas Hauzeur (violon),  Vilmos Csikos (contrebasse) et J\u00e9r\u00e9mie B\u00e9nichou (br\u00e0cs) vous pr\u00e9sentera les plus belles chansons de ce r\u00e9pertoire : certaines vous feront pleurer, d'autres danser. Dans tous les cas, venez profiter de cette soir\u00e9e avec nous ! \n\nPrix d'entr\u00e9e : librement choisi \u00b7 pay what you can \n\nPlus d'info sur la page de l'\u00e9v\u00e8nement : https:\/\/fb.me\/e\/634vBejhF  ","performers":"Marina Csik\u00f3s ; Csilla Deak (auteur-compositeur-interpr\u00e8te) ; Nicolas Hauzeur (violon) ; Vilmos Csikos (contrebasse) ; J\u00e9r\u00e9mie B\u00e9nichou (br\u00e0cs) ","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/fb.me\/e\/634vBejhF","email":"medexmuseum@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001733"},"sp":{"name":"WORKSHOP + CONCERT \u00b7 Across Hungarian borders : Roma re-creation with words & Music from Transylvania","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/fb.me\/e\/634vBejhF","email":"medexmuseum@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50001733"},"nl":{"name":"Across Hungarian borders : Roma re-creation with words & Music from Transylvania","shortdescr":"On Friday 15th September, let's cross the borders of a monolithic Hungarian identity with a workshop around languages and identity, followed by two concerts that will bring us on a journey to Transylvania, exploring the Hungarian subculture of Romania ! ","longdescr":"18.00 \u00b7 Decolonial poem writing workshop : a Hungarian-Roma (re)creation with words with Marina Csik\u00f3s (IN ENGLISH) \n\nThis workshop is for everyone who has ever found themselves in the position of \"in-betweeness\" and internal conflicts of languages, cultures, identities, places and feelings. \n\nDuration : 2 hours \u00b7 Free participation \u00b7 Register by email : medexmuseum(at)gmail.com\n\n\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\n\n20.30 \u00b7 CONCERT-OPENING : La Farkas, songwriting in Hungarian by Csilla De\u00e0k\n\n21.00 \u00b7 CONCERT - T\u00c0NCH\u00c0Z : \"Outside the borders: Hungarian Music from Transylvania\"\n\nTransylvania (\"Erd\u00e9ly\" in Hungarian) is a region of Romania, home of an important Hungarian minority, whose traditional music is very popular in Hungary. Since the 70s, Budapest people favor Erd\u00e9lyi tunes in their t\u00e0nch\u00e0z (folk balls). The band will present some of the most beautiful songs o